# Vercel builds ONLY the root Next.js marketing site. Everything below is part of
# the monorepo but is not needed for (and must not influence) the frontend build.
#
# EVERY PATTERN IS ANCHORED WITH A LEADING SLASH, and that is load-bearing.
# These behave like .gitignore rules: an unanchored `docs/` matches a directory
# named `docs` at ANY depth. When the marketing site gained on-site
# documentation at `src/app/docs/`, that rule silently excluded it from the
# upload — the build succeeded, every other route deployed, and all seven docs
# pages 404'd in production while serving 200 from an identical local build.
# Anchoring restricts each rule to the repo root, which is all it ever meant.
/backend/
/apps/
/packages/
/scripts/
/docs/
/packaging/
/.muon/
/.kiro/
/.github/
/backend.Dockerfile
/Dockerfile
/docker-compose.yml
